# Worked example run config: namespace scaling on the lab (README, "Namespace scaling").
# A shape check, not customer numbers: one in-place growth series of config-only
# namespaces with 2 Services each, grown 100 -> 200 -> 400 on ONE member (mesh size 1),
# with a probe window per scoping (none, namespace, wide) at every step, then 200
# namespaces outside the mesh (unlabeled, then labeled). About 45-55 min.
#
# Keys are config/options.env knobs (and SETUP_CONTEXTS); a flag still beats a key.
# Parsed, never sourced: KEY=value only, no $ or ` outside single quotes. This file
# drives the sweep (003), which passes the growth flags to 001, 002 and 005 itself.
#
# Plan first (no cluster contact), then run, then report one sweep:
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx> --dry-run
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx>
#   ./tests/controlplane/004-report-results.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env \
#     --results-dir tests/controlplane/results/ns-scaling-lab/sweep-<RUN_ID> --format markdown
# The series ends undiscovered (labels removed, namespaces kept). Delete them later,
# outside any measurement, allowing about 1 s per namespace (005 prints the rate):
#   ./tests/controlplane/005-cleanup.sh --contexts <mesh-a-ctx> --timeout 1200
#
# Pods-vs-config-only calibration (fills the report's REQUIRED row): the same N, K and
# scoping deployed fresh, once config-only and once with pods (N=30 x K=2 = 60 pods),
# into the same results base. Each fresh cell deletes its 30 namespaces and waits. Then
# report the base dir, which reads every sweep under it (the series above included). Each
# sweep's series keeps its own cells and fits (labelled run=<RUN_ID>), so a smoke run in
# the same base never bends the main curve; only the pods-vs-config-only and
# fresh-vs-in-place rows pair cells across sweeps:
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx> \
#     --growth fresh --namespace-counts 30 --sidecar-scopings namespace --outside-modes none --measurement-pod-counts 4
#   ./tests/controlplane/003-run-sweep.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env --contexts <mesh-a-ctx> \
#     --growth fresh --namespace-counts 30 --sidecar-scopings namespace --outside-modes none --measurement-pod-counts 4 \
#     --workload-mode pods --replica-counts 1
#   ./tests/controlplane/004-report-results.sh --config tests/controlplane/configs/ns-scaling-lab.env \
#     --results-dir tests/controlplane/results/ns-scaling-lab --format markdown
# That report lists every run it pools (run_ids, istio_versions, harness_shas) and names
# the runs of each side of the pods-vs-config-only row; it warns when the Istio version
# or harness commit differs, so run all three sweeps from one clean commit.
# The first grow step (from 0) also boots the measurement pods, so the report leaves it
# out of the per-namespace onboarding fits: those rest on the 200 and 400 steps.
#
# SETUP_CONTEXTS must list every mesh member: the memory guard samples istiod and the
# gateways on all of them, since every member ingests the Services through remote
# discovery. Keep real context names out of git: copy this file to
# tests/controlplane/configs/<name>.local.env (gitignored) and set them there:
# SETUP_CONTEXTS=<mesh-a-ctx>,<mesh-b-ctx>

# Growth series (003): K services per namespace, the ladder of N, one mesh member.
CONTROLPLANE_MESH_SIZES=1
CONTROLPLANE_SERVICES_PER_NAMESPACES=2
CONTROLPLANE_NAMESPACE_COUNTS=100,200,400
CONTROLPLANE_SIDECAR_SCOPINGS=none,namespace,wide
CONTROLPLANE_WORKLOAD_MODE=config-only
# 4 measurement pods; 4,16 adds the M-sweep (does istiod heap grow with proxied namespaces?).
CONTROLPLANE_MEASUREMENT_POD_COUNTS=4
CONTROLPLANE_OUTSIDE_NAMESPACES=200
CONTROLPLANE_OUTSIDE_MODES=unlabeled,labeled

# Windows and collection.
CONTROLPLANE_SETTLE_SEC=45
CONTROLPLANE_PROBE_SETTLE_SEC=45
CONTROLPLANE_CONFIG_DUMP_SAMPLES=4

# Safety: skip a cell projected above 70% of the istiod or gateway memory limit; keep
# the namespaces after the series (no deletion queue during the run).
CONTROLPLANE_MEM_STOP_PCT=70
CONTROLPLANE_SERIES_RETIRE=undiscover

# Results under the repo root (gitignored); a sweep adds sweep-<RUN_ID>/.
CONTROLPLANE_RESULTS_DIR=tests/controlplane/results/ns-scaling-lab
